Job description:
PT Asuransi Raksa Pratikara is looking for a software engineer to help expand and enhance the company’s portfolio of software applications. Raksa’s portfolio of applications encompasses a wide range of software, including consumer-facing web applications, B2B APIs, internal servers and mobile native apps. Additionally, Raksa’s applications are deployed both on-premises as well as in the cloud. As a result, the ideal candidate will have a strong interest in learning about and working on a wide range of applications and technologies. While there is no requirement for a specific programming language for this position, experience with PHP, JavaScript/TypeScript or Python are a plus. Additionally, experience with NextJS/React, Android/iOS and serverless cloud architectures are also positives. Since Raksa’s software engineers work in small teams and utilize an agile development workflow, the ideal candidate should enjoy working in a fast-paced and collaborative environment.


Requirements :

S1 fresh graduate from a reputable university with a minimum GPA of 2.75;

Minimum of 1 year of experience in software development using any programming language;

Strong understanding of fundamental software engineering concepts, algorithms and design patterns;

Experience developing mobile applications (iOS and/or Android) is a plus;

Experience working with cloud platforms (e.g., Amazon AWS, Google Compute Cloud or Microsoft Azure) and developing serverless applications is a plus;

Passionate about learning and using new technologies in a fast-paced environment;

Excellent collaborative and communication skills.

C# Backend Engineer (API Integration)

1. Responsibilities

1. Develop and maintain backend systems based on C# (ASP.NET Core);

2. Integrate with third-party platform APIs (e.g., TikTok, Shopify);

3. Design and implement core business workflows (content moderation, task

processing, data handling, etc.);

4. Handle data collection, processing, and storage related to video/content;

5. Participate in system architecture design to improve scalability and stability;

6. Develop scheduled tasks, asynchronous jobs, and data synchronization processes;

7. Collaborate closely with frontend engineers and product managers to deliver

features efficiently.

2. Requirements

1. Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or related field is preferred;

2. 3+ years of backend development experience;

3. Proficient in C# and familiar with ASP.NET Core (.NET 6 or above);

4. Strong understanding of RESTful API design and development;

5. Hands-on experience with third-party API integration (required);

6. Familiar with OAuth2 authentication and authorization mechanisms;

7. Experience with relational databases such as MySQL or PostgreSQL;

8. Familiar with Redis (caching, distributed locks, etc.);

9. Experience with NoSQL databases such as MongoDB is a plus;

10. Familiar with asynchronous programming (async/await) and task scheduling tools

(e.g., Hangfire / Quartz.NET);

11. Experience with message queues (e.g., RabbitMQ / Kafka) is a plus;

12. Basic knowledge of Linux and experience with Docker is preferred.

3. Preferred Qualifications

1. Experience with TikTok API or e-commerce platform APIs (e.g., Shopify);

2. Experience building content platforms, moderation systems, or distribution

systems;

3. Experience with data analytics, reporting, or commission systems;

4. Experience handling high-concurrency or large-scale data processing;

5. Experience in system architecture design or owning end-to-end projects.

4. We Expect You To Have

• Strong coding standards and engineering practices;

• Excellent problem-solving skills;

• Good communication and teamwork abilities;

• Strong execution and willingness to learn new technologies.

5. Keywords

C# / ASP.NET Core / API Integration / TikTok API / Shopify API / OAuth2 / Redis /

MongoDB / Async Jobs / Data Processing

About the job

Cove started with renting coliving spaces. Now we’ve expanded to more than just coliving spaces, providing flexibility for comfortable and enjoyable long term or short term stays in our beautiful properties. With over 6000 rooms across Singapore and Indonesia, we’re living our mission and growing our homes in South Korea and Japan.

Believing in the power of a team, we aim to build the leading tech flexible living platform in Asia Pacific, providing high quality and community-centric accommodations. Here we also encourage authenticity and fun to fully embrace being human in a driven and result focused environment to make things happen and ensure the dream becomes a reality.

Job Title: Data Engineer (Data Infrastructure & Business Insights)

Job Type: Full-time

Reports To: Head of Engineering

Location: Remote (~GMT+8)

What You’ll Be Doing


Design, build, and maintain efficient ETL/ELT processes and reliable data pipelines in dbt and BigQuery, integrating data from a variety of sources (MongoDB, SQL, Google Sheets, Google Analytics, APIs, etc.);
Build and maintain dashboards and visualizations in Looker Studio and other BI tools;
Ensure data quality, consistency, and accessibility across the organization, implement data quality controls;
Proactively collaborate with different stakeholders across operations, sales, finance and tech to clarify requirements and answer data-related questions.


What Makes You a Great Fit


5 years of experience in data engineering, analytics engineering, or data analytics roles in a fast-paced or startup environment;
Strong communication skills and the ability to collaborate effectively with non-technical stakeholders to translate business needs into actionable data solutions;
Strong proficiency in SQL and Excel, experience with BigQuery or similar cloud data warehouses. Familiarity with MongoDB is a plus;
Experience with Python for data processing or automation (knowledge of other programming languages is a plus);
Solid understanding of data modeling and database design principles;
Hands-on experience with data visualization and BI tools, especially Looker Studio;
Proficient git user;
BS in Mathematics, Economics, Computer Science, Information Management or Statistics;
Fluent in written and spoken English.


This Role Might Not Be a Good Fit If


You prefer to focus purely on coding and don’t enjoy collaborating or communicating with non-technical teams. This role requires frequent interaction with business stakeholders to understand their needs and translate them into data solutions;
You find it stressful to manage multiple tasks at once. Our data requests can come from several teams simultaneously, and priorities may shift quickly — flexibility and context-switching are part of the job.


Salary Range

1500-2300 SGD (20-30M IDR) depending on experience.

Frontend Engineer (Vue / Admin System)

Responsibilities

1. Develop and maintain frontend systems based on Vue;

2. Build and optimize admin dashboards (content review, data dashboards, task

management, etc.);

3. Integrate with backend APIs and implement data display and interaction logic;

4. Participate in UI structure design and user experience optimization;

5. Continuously improve frontend performance and code quality;




Requirements

1. At least 2 years of frontend development experience;

2. Strong proficiency in JavaScript / HTML / CSS;

3. Proficient in Vue (Vue 3 preferred) with solid component-based development skills;

4. Familiar with UI frameworks such as Element Plus or Ant Design Vue;

5. Experienced in API integration (Axios / Fetch) and frontend-backend separation;

6. Familiar with Git or other version control tools;

7. Good coding standards and development practices;




Core Competencies (Must Have)

1. Experience in building admin/backend management systems (key requirement);

2. Ability to independently implement common features such as lists, filtering, pagination, and state management;

3. Ability to understand business workflows (e.g., review processes, state transitions) and implement corresponding UI logic;

4. Ability to independently integrate with backend APIs and complete feature development;




Preferred Qualifications

1. Experience with data dashboards or charting tools (e.g., ECharts);

2. Experience with permission management systems (roles/menus);

3. Experience in e-commerce or content platforms;

4. Experience in frontend performance optimization;


Keywords

Vue3 / Admin System / API Integration / Data Dashboard / Content Review System

Staf IT

Pendidikan

S1 Teknologi Informasi

Pengalaman

Memiliki Pengalaman Kerja > 2 Tahun

Kemampuan Teknis

Berpengalaman dalam pengembangan sistem dan website menggunakan PHP dan Laravel framework;

Memahami konsep MVC, OOP, dan RESTful API;

Berpengalaman dalam merancang, menulis dan mengoptimalkan kueri SQL pada MySQL & PostgreSQL;

Mampu menganalisa sistem dan pengelolaan sistem aplikasi, infrastruktur jaringan dan server;

Berpengalaman mengimplementasikan keamanan sistem dan backup data serta troubleshooting perangkat keras, perangkat lunak, dan jaringan;

Berpengalaman menyusun laporan sistem dan melakukan evaluasi teknologi informasi serta mengelola sistem dan database lembaga.

Key Responsibilities

Mengelola dan memastikan operasional, aplikasi, server, dan infrastruktur IT organisasi berjalan optimal

Memberikan dukungan teknis serta menangani troubleshooting perangkat keras, perangkat lunak, dan jaringan;

Mengelola keamanan sistem dan data organisasi serta Menyusun laporan kinerja dan evluasi sistem IT.

Deskripsi Pekerjaan What you'll do
Develop and Implement Dashboarding Best Practices: Lead the standardization and centralization of dashboarding frameworks, ensuring consistent, insightful, and user-friendly visualizations across teams;
Empower Self-Serve Analytics: Collaborate with stakeholders to design and deploy scalable, intuitive analytics solutions and tools, enabling teams to access and interpret data independently;
Optimize ETL Pipelines for Scalability: Build and maintain efficient ETL processes to ensure reliable, accurate, and timely delivery of data to support analytics and reporting needs;
Develop and maintain reliable data models to support key business metrics;
Create and implement processes to ensure data quality and accuracy;
Handle data discovery, exploration, and insights generation for business and product improvements;
Experience in coaching, guiding and leading projects alongside junior team members.
What you'll need
4+ years of data analytics experience;
Bachelor’s degree in System Information, Computer Science, Mathematics, Statistics, or related fields from a reputable university;
Advanced SQL and data manipulation skills;
Data wrangling experience with Python/R;
Advanced Excel knowledge;
Good experience with one or more databases like Snowflake, BigQuery, Redshift, Postgres, Oracle, Teradata, MySQL etc;
Excellent data visualization skills using Tableau/Looker or other data visualization tools;
Detail-oriented with a focus on accuracy.

Sabemos que carreiras podem ser tão diferentes quanto as próprias pessoas. Por isso, na EY, você terá a liberdade, as ferramentas e as condições para se desenvolver e construir uma carreira tão única quanto você.

Em Tech Financial Services (Tech FSO), estamos construindo um mundo de negócios melhor apoiando as necessidades e desafios tecnológicos dos nossos clientes do segmento financeiro (Mercado de Capitais, Bancos, Fintechs, Seguros e Gestão de Ativos). Entregamos soluções sob medida com base nas necessidades específicas de cada negócio, a partir de uma equipe multidisciplinar de especialistas com diferentes perfis, como especialistas em Dados, UX, até analistas de negócios e scrum masters. 

#TechEY

Qual será o seu papel nesse propósito?

Como Desenvolvedor(a) Cobol você irá atuar em cliente de grande porte, com oportunidade de crescimento em frentes diversas na área de dados voltados para o segmento financeiro. Você poderá contar com ferramentas, conhecimentos e oportunidades para avançar e estar pronto/a para construir um mundo de negócios melhor para nossas pessoas, clientes e as comunidades que nos apoiam.

Por que você?

Se você é apaixonado(a) por dados, colaboração e tem as seguintes qualificações, queremos você em nossa equipe:

Formação completa/cursando nas áreas de Tecnologia, Ciências da Computação, Análise de Sistemas,Matemática, Estatística, Engenharias e ou correlatas;

Experiência em linguagens de programação, principalmente Java e atualizado com as tendências e tecnologias de mercado;

Proficiência em Programação Cobol, JCL e Natural;

Ambientes de Desenvolvimento: Experiência com ambientes mainframe, como IBM z/OS;

Ferramentas de Banco de Dados: Conhecimento em DB2, Oracle ou outros bancos de dados relacionais, além de habilidades em SQL;

Ferramentas de Depuração: Familiaridade com ferramentas de depuração e análise de desempenho específicas para Cobol;

Controle de Versão: Experiência com sistemas de controle de versão, como Git ou SVN, para gerenciamento de código-fonte;

Metodologias Ágeis: Habilidade em trabalhar com metodologias ágeis, como Scrum ou Kanban, para desenvolvimento colaborativo.

Inglês técnico.

Desejável:

Serão considerados diferenciais:

Experiência em integração de sistemas legados, familiaridade com ferramentas de desenvolvimento para Cobol, JCL e Natural;

Conhecimento em metodologias ágeis, certificações relevantes e habilidades em testes e garantia de qualidade de softwares;

Certificações: IBM Certified Application Developer - COBOL Certified Professional in Business Analysis (CPBA) Micro Focus Certified Professional - COBOL.

Principais Responsabilidades:

Desenvolvimento e Manutenção: Criar e manter aplicações em Cobol, JCL e Natural, garantindo a funcionalidade e eficiência do sistema;

Análise de Requisitos: Colaborar com equipes de negócios para entender e traduzir requisitos em soluções técnicas;

Integração de Sistemas: Trabalhar na integração de sistemas legados com novas tecnologias e plataformas;

Testes e Validação: Realizar testes de software para garantir a qualidade e a robustez das aplicações desenvolvidas;

Documentação: Produzir e manter documentação técnica e de processos para referência futura e conformidade.

O que oferecemos: Vale Alimentação, Vale Refeição, Vale Transporte, Plano de saúde, Assistência odontológica, Universidade Corporativa e outros benefícios Educacionais, Wellhub, PLR, e muito mais. Clique aqui e conheça nosso universo de benefícios.

Quem somos: Somos uma das maiores empresas de serviços do mundo, em Auditoria, Consultoria, Impostos, Estratégia e Transações, orientados à Tecnologia. Com presença em mais de 150 países, aqui você terá a oportunidade de viver as experiências excepcionais que só a EY pode oferecer, com alcance global, cultura inclusiva e tecnologia para se tornar a sua melhor versão.

Aqui, acreditamos que a força que impulsiona a inovação vem da diversidade de pessoas e ideias. Segundo o Great Place to Work 2023, somos a melhor empresa para pessoas LGBTQ+ do Brasil, e a 2a melhor empresa para Mulheres e para Pessoas Pretas. Assim, você poderá fazer parte de nossos programas e grupos que, juntos a inúmeras iniciativas internas, apoiam nossa constante busca pela equidade.

Quer se sentir desafiado/a, motivado/a e valorizado/a todos os dias? Inspirar mudanças e deixar um legado? Faça parte do nosso time e ajude-nos na construção de um mundo de negócios melhor!

Saiba mais sobre como é trabalhar na EY:

Carreiras na EY LinkedIn @EY Instagram @eybrasilcarreiras     

Oportunidade disponível em modelo presencial (com flexibilidade para o remoto) nos escritórios da EY Brasil.

About the job

Join Hostinger, and we’ll grow fast! 🚀
We’re shaping the future of online success - powered by AI and driven by people. With 900+ talented professionals and over 5 million clients in 150 countries, we help creators and entrepreneurs bring their ideas to life faster and easier than ever before.

Our mission: To provide tools that help individuals and small businesses succeed online faster and easier.

Our culture: Guided by 10 company principles.
Our formula for success: Customer obsession, innovative products, and talented teams.

Your role at Hostinger
System Administrator Manager in the Product team. As part of Hostinger's Product team, you'll lead the SysAdmin Indonesian team. While you are technically credible and know the details of what engineers work on, your time will be spent safeguarding your team’s health, hiring world-class people, and putting them in the best position to succeed. You will own the delivery of product commitments and always look to improve productivity. In this role, you'll collaborate closely with Lithuanian and Brazilian SysAdmin teams, developers, engineers, and product managers.

Curious to learn more? Connect with your team: Eimantas Šerpenskas, Engineering manager

Your skills and experience:



You have been supporting enterprise-level Linux environments, resolving technical system problems, including product, database, and linux optimization, for 3+ years;
You have been technically leading and mentoring an engineering team for 1+ years;
You understand the on-premises infrastructure and cloud-based systems;
Your English skills are C1 - C2;
You are a constant learner who loves Linux and is truly passionate about IT, engineering, and people





Your day-to-day:



Keep Hostinger’s Web Hosting Monitoring team in an always-ready state;
Provide long-term engineering solutions for Hostinger’s Web Hosting services;
Coach, onboard new team members and provide day-to-day team leadership and supervision;
Foster technical decision-making on the team but make final decisions when necessary;
Analyze system performance and solve technical issues;
Plan and deliver team KPIs and find ways to increase team efficiency and performance;
Coordinate and automate deployment, monitoring, maintenance, and support of systems and services;
Identify service problems from the client’s side and advise colleagues on difficult cases;
Monitor and optimize Hostinger service performance using Grafana, Kibana, Elasticsearch, Prometheus, Ansible, and other tools;
Ensure uptime of core services;
Make sure retention strategies and downtime handling procedures are followed;





Benefits for you:



🚀 360 Growth: We provide limitless learning opportunities: access to platforms like Reforge and CoachHub, global conferences, physical and digital libraries, and feedback culture. Advance your career with internal mobility and grow with a team eager to share knowledge and support your success
🎯 Freedom & responsibility: Work on your terms: from a modern office in Yogyakarta or your home office. Enjoy flexibility in managing your schedule and bring your ideas to life in a fast-paced, dynamic environment
💪 Wellness simplified: Your health comes first with private insurance, Headspace subscriptions, recharge leave, and regular health checks. Join sports, arts, and hobby clubs or simply enjoy the balance of a lifestyle that prioritizes wellness
🎉 Work hard - play hard: Recognize hard work with company events, Town Hall, Meet the Client initiatives, team-buildings, and workations. Celebrate life’s big moments with milestone gifts for weddings, new parenthood, and graduations





We’re always looking for experienced talent to raise the bar. If you’re excited about the role but the listed salary range doesn’t align with your expectations, we still encourage you to apply - we’re open to adjusting compensation based on the impact and value you bring.

Get ready to take your personal and professional growth to new heights! Join Hostinger today and be part of our journey 🚀
